Template: supermon-ng/configure-apache
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Configure Apache for Supermon-ng?
 Automatically enable required Apache modules and reload Apache. With the
 default subdirectory layout (/supermon-ng) this installs a global
 /etc/apache2/conf-available/supermon-ng.conf that works under the existing
 default sites (Debian or ASL3 appliance), which are left enabled. With
 APP_BASE_PATH=/ it installs a dedicated site under
 /etc/apache2/sites-available/ instead.
 .
 Choose "No" if you use nginx or manage Apache vhosts yourself.

Template: supermon-ng/disable-default-sites
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Disable default Apache sites (APP_BASE_PATH=/ only)?
 When Supermon-ng uses a dedicated site at the web root, disable the Debian
 default sites (000-default and default-ssl) so it can serve HTTP/HTTPS on
 ports 80 and 443. Ignored for the default /supermon-ng layout.

Template: supermon-ng/refresh-apache-site
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Regenerate Apache site configuration?
 With APP_BASE_PATH=/, replace /etc/apache2/sites-available/supermon-ng.conf
 with a newly generated configuration from your current .env settings. With
 the /supermon-ng layout, which needs no site, disable it and move it to
 supermon-ng.conf.bak.
 .
 Only choose "Yes" if you want to discard manual edits to that file.
